{
	"title": "Somme et produit des racines",
	"description": "x₁ + x₂ = −b/a et x₁x₂ = c/a sans calculer les racines",
	"grades": ["1_SPE"],
	"theme": "Fonctions",
	"domain": "Polynôme du second degré",
	"status": "draft",
	"subdomain": "Racines",
	"level": 5,
	"delay": 40,
	"shared": {
		"blankDefaults": {
			"acceptDecimal": true
		}
	},
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Le polynôme $P(x)={{eval:ax^2+bx+c}}$ a deux racines $x_1$ et $x_2$. Sans les calculer, détermine leur somme et leur produit.\n\n$x_1+x_2=?$ et $x_1\\times x_2=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "1"
				},
				{
					"name": "b",
					"expression": "1..9;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "1..9;±"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["b^2-4*a*c > 0"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:-b}}"
				},
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{c}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Le discriminant vaut $\\Delta={{eval:b;()}}^2-4\\times{{eval:a;()}}\\times{{eval:c;()}}={{eval:b^2-4*a*c}}>0$ : les deux racines existent.",
					"Quand un trinôme $ax^2+bx+c$ a deux racines, $x_1+x_2=-\\dfrac{b}{a}$ et $x_1\\times x_2=\\dfrac{c}{a}$.",
					"Ici $a=1$ : $x_1+x_2=-b={{eval:-b}}$ et $x_1\\times x_2=c={{c}}$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Le polynôme $P(x)={{eval:ax^2+bx+c}}$ a deux racines $x_1$ et $x_2$. Sans les calculer, détermine leur somme et leur produit.\n\n$x_1+x_2=?$ et $x_1\\times x_2=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "2..5;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "b",
					"expression": "1..9;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "1..9;±"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["b^2-4*a*c > 0"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:-b/a}}"
				},
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:c/a}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Le discriminant vaut $\\Delta={{eval:b;()}}^2-4\\times{{eval:a;()}}\\times{{eval:c;()}}={{eval:b^2-4*a*c}}>0$ : les deux racines existent.",
					"Quand un trinôme $ax^2+bx+c$ a deux racines, $x_1+x_2=-\\dfrac{b}{a}$ et $x_1\\times x_2=\\dfrac{c}{a}$.",
					"$$x_1+x_2=-\\dfrac{b}{a}=\\dfrac{ {{eval:-b}} }{ {{a}} }={{eval:-b/a}} \\qquad x_1\\times x_2=\\dfrac{c}{a}=\\dfrac{ {{c}} }{ {{a}} }={{eval:c/a}}$$"
				]
			}
		}
	],
